    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0423" n="341" xml:id="pg341"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the British Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I beg to acknowledge
                    receipt of your personal note of the 16th instant, relative to the Kanré-Lahun
                    boundary question, and to say in reply that the Department on the 19th instant
                    cabled the American minister at Monrovia to inform the Liberian Government that
                    the prompt settlement of the question of the Kanré-Lahun boundary on the basis
                    of the exchange of Kanré-Lahun for the Morro-Mano territory and £4,000 as the
                    cost of developing the new territory would be favorably regarded by this
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
